{"id":"chatcmpl-0fe5b588-70ef-4fe3-a70e-dbc178ce9da0","object":"chat.completion","created":1795251750,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first approach to medical image interpretation: rather than answering directly from visual inspection, the agent cross-checks findings using an expert tool and a grounding tool, then resolves laterality by anchoring to an explicit image marker. The key insight is that spatial orientation (left vs. right) must be confirmed against a reference marker, not assumed from image position, since radiological images are conventionally displayed mirrored relative to the patient.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a question hinges on spatial laterality (left/right), always anchor the finding to an explicit orientation marker in the image rather than assuming image-side equals patient-side.\",\n    \"Use a domain-expert tool to obtain an independent interpretation before committing to an answer, especially when options are near-mirror alternatives.\",\n    \"Corroborate a visual claim with a grounding/localization tool that returns coordinates, then map those coordinates to the correct anatomical side using the orientation marker.\",\n    \"For binary option sets that differ only by a single attribute (e.g., side), explicitly state the discriminating evidence in the final reasoning to justify the choice.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Confirm laterality against the image's orientation marker (e.g., 'L'/'R') before answering; treat image-left as patient-right unless the marker says otherwise.\",\n    \"Binary-choice visual QA\": \"Identify the single attribute that distinguishes the options, then gather targeted evidence specifically for that attribute rather than re-describing the whole image.\",\n    \"Tool-assisted verification\": \"Chain an expert-interpretation tool with a localization tool; agreement between a semantic judgment and grounded coordinates increases confidence.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Locate and read the orientation marker (L/R) in the image before deciding laterality.\",\n    \"Confirm that the grounded coordinates of the finding fall on the correct side relative to the orientation marker.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":469,"total_tokens":870,"completion_tokens":401,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":469},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":401}}}